Author:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Mon Oct 12 14:11:07 2026 -0500
Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Mon Oct 12 14:11:07 2026 -0500

    fix(api): roll queue ETA estimate over recent solves. Addresses DF-OFF-BY-ONE-38.
    
    Queue.AvgSolveTime averaged completed_at-started_at over ALL completed
    entries, so months of old, faster solves dominated the mean and the API
    silently underquoted current waits (live observation: a ~6m35s solve
    quoted as 3m33s).
    
    The estimate is now a rolling mean over the 20 most recently completed
    solves (bounded SQL subquery, ORDER BY completed_at DESC LIMIT 20).
    Fallback semantics are unchanged: an empty window still returns 0 and
    handlers fall back to the 30s per-job default; labs with fewer than 20
    completions average what they have. estimateTime caps, position rules,
    and pending/in_progress/terminal wire shapes are untouched.
    
    Tests (RED-proven against the pre-fix all-history query):
    - TestQueue_AvgSolveTime_RecentWindow: stale 40s history + 3 recent
      400s solves yields the 94s window mean, never the ~87s all-history
      mean.
    - TestQueue_AvgSolveTime_WindowDropsOldest: with window+1 completions
      the oldest outlier drops out of the sample.
    - TestQueue_AvgSolveTime_NoCompletes: no completions still returns 0
      (fallback contract, no fabricated number).
    - TestSubmit_EstimatedTimeUsesRecentWindow: submit quotes 1m34s from
      the window (raw-JSON key asserted), never the 1m27s all-history
      quote; pending/in_progress/terminal detail semantics and
      /api/v1/stats avg_solve_time preserved.
    
    Docs: api-reference.md, integration.md, and openapi.yaml now describe
    the estimator honestly as a rolling 20-solve window.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
